regexec.c: the regset search reuses its memory

onig_regset_search allocated and freed three arrays on every call, and in
ONIG_REGSET_POSITION_LEAD mode every match_at it ran, for each regex at
each position, allocated a match stack. With this patch, the set keeps the
arrays (tm_mps, tm_msas, tm_sr) and one match stack (tm_stk) between
searches, and clears a region only when its regex needs a cleared one.

What a search finds is unchanged. The region of a regex that did not match
keeps the values of an earlier search; the port reads only the region of
the regex that the search returns.

See rust/vendor/README.md.

